# The ledger of `image`: what Go's `image`, `image/color`, `image/color/palette`
# and `image/draw` (Go 1.27) and Python's Pillow let a program do with an
# image in memory, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. The file
# formats are the subpackages' own ledgers: `image/png`, `image/jpeg`,
# `image/gif`, `image/bmp`, `image/netpbm`.
#
# Go's lists are this machine's, 2026-11-18: `go doc -all` on each package.
# Pillow is not installed here and nothing may be installed, so its names are
# those of its documented public API (`Image`, `ImageDraw`, `ImageOps`,
# `ImageChops`, `ImageFilter`, `ImageEnhance`, `ImageStat`, `ImageColor`,
# `ImagePalette`, `ImageSequence`, `ImageCms`, `ImageFont`, `ImageGrab`,
# `ImageShow`), not read by `dir()`: a question rather than a measurement,
# and no expected value of the tests comes from it. Rust's standard library
# has no image, so its line is `-` in every block. The expected values of the
# tests were observed from Go on 2026-11-18 (gray from colour, the web-safe
# palette); where Go has no such function (resizing, turning by any angle,
# drawing), the tests hold the properties the documentation states and small
# cases computed by hand from the definition, and say so.

capability image/value  an image held in memory: its size, how a pixel is held, its bytes
  heroes  image.Image, image.Format
  go      Image, RGBA, RGBA64, NRGBA, NRGBA64, Gray, Gray16, Alpha, Alpha16, CMYK, Paletted, YCbCr, NYCbCrA, Config, RGBA64Image, PalettedImage, draw.Image, draw.RGBA64Image, and their fields Pix, Stride, Rect, Palette, Y, Cb, Cr, A, YStride, CStride, AStride, SubsampleRatio
  rust    -
  python  Image.Image, Image.mode, Image.size, Image.width, Image.height, Image.info
  note    eight formats: gray, gray and alpha, RGB, RGBA, at 8 or 16 bits a sample, 16 bits held high byte first as Go's Gray16 and PNG hold them; alpha straight as Go's NRGBA and Pillow's RGBA, never premultiplied as Go's RGBA. An image begins at 0, 0 and has no stride of its own: a row is width × pixel bytes. CMYK, YCbCr, alpha alone and Pillow's 1-bit, 32-bit integer and float modes are not formats here; their block is below

capability image/new  a blank image of a size and format
  heroes  image.blank
  go      NewRGBA, NewRGBA64, NewNRGBA, NewNRGBA64, NewGray, NewGray16, NewAlpha, NewAlpha16, NewCMYK, NewPaletted, NewYCbCr, NewNYCbCrA, NewUniform, Uniform, Black, White, Transparent, Opaque, Uniform.At, Uniform.Bounds, Uniform.ColorModel, Uniform.Convert, Uniform.Opaque, Uniform.RGBA, Uniform.RGBA64At
  rust    -
  python  Image.new, Image.linear_gradient, Image.radial_gradient
  note    every sample 0, black and transparent, as Go's New functions make one; Pillow's colour argument is `fill_rect` over the whole image. A Uniform, an image of one colour without bounds, is a colour here: `fill_rect` paints one. The gradients are pending under image/generate

capability image/generate  images made from a formula: gradients, noise, a Mandelbrot set
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.linear_gradient, Image.radial_gradient, Image.effect_noise, Image.effect_mandelbrot, Image.effect_spread
  note    -

capability image/from-bytes  an image made from bytes the program holds, and its bytes read out
  heroes  image.from_pixels, image.Image
  go      Pix fields of every image type, PixOffset, RGBA.PixOffset, Gray.PixOffset (each type's), YCbCr.YOffset, YCbCr.COffset, NYCbCrA.AOffset
  rust    -
  python  Image.frombytes, Image.frombuffer, Image.tobytes, Image.fromarray, Image.__array_interface__
  note    the bytes are `Image.pixels`, read and written directly; `from_pixels` checks their count. fromarray and the array interface are numpy's, which has no counterpart

capability image/valid  whether an image holds the bytes its size says
  heroes  image.is_valid
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.verify
  note    a record built directly may say one size and hold another; every function asks this first and aborts, the caller having been able to ask. Pillow's verify checks a file, which each decoder here does as it reads

capability image/limits  a limit on the size a decoder may allocate, against decompression bombs
  heroes  image.Limits, image.default_limits, image.check_limits, image.LIMIT, image.DEFAULT_MAX_WIDTH, image.DEFAULT_MAX_HEIGHT, image.DEFAULT_MAX_PIXELS
  go      DecodeConfig (read first, then the program decides)
  rust    -
  python  Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS, Image.DecompressionBombError, Image.DecompressionBombWarning
  note    every decoder takes Limits and fails `limit` before it allocates; Go has no limit (its documentation says to call DecodeConfig first), Pillow warns at MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS and fails at twice it. The defaults here are 65,536 a side and 2^26 pixels, 256 MiB of RGBA: a decision, not Pillow's number, which could not be read on this machine

capability image/format-facts  what a format holds: channels, bits, bytes, alpha
  heroes  image.channels_of, image.bits_of, image.pixel_bytes_of, image.has_alpha, image.format_with
  go      Image.ColorModel, Opaque (each type's), RGBA.Opaque, Model
  rust    -
  python  Image.getbands, Image.mode, Image.has_transparency_data, ImageMode.getmode
  note    Opaque, whether every pixel is opaque, is a scan a program writes with `samples_at`; it is not offered apart

capability image/pixel-read  one pixel read, as a colour or as its samples
  heroes  image.color_at, image.samples_at, image.Color
  go      Image.At, RGBA.RGBAAt, RGBA64.RGBA64At, NRGBA.NRGBAAt, NRGBA64.NRGBA64At, Gray.GrayAt, Gray16.Gray16At, Alpha.AlphaAt, Alpha16.Alpha16At, CMYK.CMYKAt, YCbCr.YCbCrAt, NYCbCrA.NYCbCrAAt, Paletted.ColorIndexAt, RGBA64Image.RGBA64At (each type's), color.Color, color.Color.RGBA, color.RGBA, color.RGBA64, color.NRGBA, color.NRGBA64, color.Gray, color.Gray16, color.Alpha, color.Alpha16, color.Black, color.White, color.Transparent, color.Opaque, and each colour type's RGBA method
  rust    -
  python  Image.getpixel, Image.getdata, Image.load, PixelAccess, Image.getchannel
  note    `color_at` answers 8 bits a channel, a 16-bit sample by its high byte as Go converts it; `samples_at` answers the samples exactly, 16 bits included. A position outside the image aborts, as an index past the end does

capability image/pixel-write  one pixel written
  heroes  image.set_color, image.set_samples
  go      Set, SetRGBA, SetRGBA64, SetNRGBA, SetNRGBA64, SetGray, SetGray16, SetAlpha, SetAlpha16, SetCMYK, SetYCbCr, SetNYCbCrA, Paletted.SetColorIndex (each type's)
  rust    -
  python  Image.putpixel, Image.putdata
  note    a colour written into gray takes Go's luma; the pixel is replaced, never blended (Pillow's putpixel, Go's Set)

capability image/convert  an image held in another format
  heroes  image.convert
  go      color.Model, color.ModelFunc, color.RGBAModel, color.RGBA64Model, color.NRGBAModel, color.NRGBA64Model, color.GrayModel, color.Gray16Model, color.AlphaModel, color.Alpha16Model, Model.Convert
  rust    -
  python  Image.convert
  note    gray from colour is Go's GrayModel, (19595 R + 38470 G + 7471 B + 32768) >> 16 on 16-bit values, observed from Go on two colours and Gray16Model on one; Pillow's ITU-R 601-2 luma differs by at most one. Alpha dropped keeps the colour (Pillow's convert from RGBA to RGB); Go's models composite over black, which is `flatten` here. 16 bits become 8 by the high byte, as Go converts

capability image/flatten  alpha blended over a background colour and dropped
  heroes  image.flatten
  go      draw.Draw over a Uniform (draw.Over)
  rust    -
  python  Image.alpha_composite onto Image.new, Image.convert with a background pasted first
  note    each colour weighted by its alpha, rounded

capability image/colour-spaces  CMYK, YCbCr, Lab, HSV and other colour spaces
  heroes  pending
  go      color.CMYK, color.CMYKModel, color.CMYKToRGB, color.RGBToCMYK, color.YCbCr, color.YCbCrModel, color.YCbCrToRGB, color.RGBToYCbCr, color.NYCbCrA, color.NYCbCrAModel, YCbCrSubsampleRatio, YCbCrSubsampleRatio444, YCbCrSubsampleRatio422, YCbCrSubsampleRatio420, YCbCrSubsampleRatio440, YCbCrSubsampleRatio411, YCbCrSubsampleRatio410, YCbCrSubsampleRatio.String, CMYK, YCbCr, NYCbCrA
  rust    -
  python  Image.convert("CMYK"), Image.convert("YCbCr"), Image.convert("LAB"), Image.convert("HSV")
  note    `image/jpeg` turns YCbCr into RGB as it reads, by JFIF's equations; a format of four samples other than RGBA, and the conversions, would need a design of their own

capability image/colour-management  ICC profiles applied: one colour space into another
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageCms, ImageCms.profileToProfile, ImageCms.buildTransform, ImageCms.applyTransform, ImageCms.createProfile, ImageCms.getOpenProfile
  note    `image/jpeg` and `image/png` read the profile's bytes (Jpeg.icc, a kept iCCP chunk); applying one is a colour engine, a package of its own

capability image/crop  a rectangle of an image as an image
  heroes  image.crop
  go      SubImage (each type's), Rectangle, Rect, Point, Pt, ZR, ZP, Rectangle.Add, Rectangle.Sub, Rectangle.Inset, Rectangle.Intersect, Rectangle.Union, Rectangle.Empty, Rectangle.Eq, Rectangle.Overlaps, Rectangle.In, Rectangle.Canon, Rectangle.Dx, Rectangle.Dy, Rectangle.Size, Rectangle.At, Rectangle.Bounds, Rectangle.ColorModel, Rectangle.RGBA64At, Rectangle.String, Rectangle.Mul, Point.Add, Point.Sub, Point.Mul, Point.Div, Point.In, Point.Mod, Point.Eq, Point.String
  rust    -
  python  Image.crop, ImageOps.crop
  note    a copy, where Go's SubImage shares the pixels: no value aliases another here. A rectangle outside the image fails `invalid`; Pillow pads it with zeros. The rectangle and point arithmetic is four numbers a program computes itself, x, y, width and height being what every function takes

capability image/flip-and-quarter-turns  mirrored, turned by quarters, transposed, exactly
  heroes  image.flip_horizontal, image.flip_vertical, image.rotate_90, image.rotate_180, image.rotate_270, image.transpose, image.transverse
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.transpose, Image.Transpose.FLIP_LEFT_RIGHT, FLIP_TOP_BOTTOM, ROTATE_90, ROTATE_180, ROTATE_270, TRANSPOSE, TRANSVERSE, ImageOps.flip, ImageOps.mirror
  note    rotate_90 is counter-clockwise, as Pillow's ROTATE_90 is

capability image/orientation  an image shown upright by its EXIF orientation
  heroes  image.apply_orientation
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageOps.exif_transpose
  note    the eight orientations as Pillow maps them to transposes; `image/jpeg` reads the orientation

capability image/rotate  an image turned by any angle
  heroes  image.rotate
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.rotate (angle, resample, expand, center, translate, fillcolor)
  note    about the centre, counter-clockwise as Pillow; a multiple of 90 is moved whole, so it is exact. Pillow's center and translate are pending under image/transform. Tested by properties (a flat image stays flat, the size an expansion takes, the corners left to the background) and small cases by hand: no reference on this machine turns an image

capability image/resize  an image scaled, under a resampling filter
  heroes  image.resize, image.Resampling
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.resize, Image.Resampling, NEAREST, BOX, BILINEAR, HAMMING, BICUBIC, LANCZOS, Image.reduce
  note    the six filters of Pillow, each widened by the scale where it shrinks so every pixel counts, and alpha premultiplied, as Pillow's documentation describes; the weights are computed in floats, so a sample may differ from Pillow's by one, unmeasured since Pillow is not here. Pillow's box argument is `crop` first; reduce is `resize` with `box`. Tested by properties and by the weights of the kernels computed by hand

capability image/thumbnail  an image made to fit a size, its proportions kept
  heroes  image.thumbnail
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.thumbnail, ImageOps.contain, ImageOps.fit, ImageOps.pad, ImageOps.cover, ImageOps.scale
  note    never enlarged, each side rounded and at least 1. fit, pad and cover are a thumbnail and a crop or a paste, which a program composes

capability image/transform  affine, perspective and mesh transforms
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.transform, Image.Transform.AFFINE, EXTENT, PERSPECTIVE, QUAD, MESH, ImageTransform
  note    -

capability image/paste  one image written into another
  heroes  image.paste
  go      draw.Draw, draw.Src, draw.Op
  rust    -
  python  Image.paste
  note    the source is converted to the destination's format and replaces what was there, alpha and all; what falls outside is dropped

capability image/composite  one image laid over another by its alpha
  heroes  image.composite
  go      draw.Draw, draw.DrawMask, draw.Over, draw.Drawer, Drawer.Draw
  rust    -
  python  Image.alpha_composite, Image.paste with a mask, Image.composite
  note    Porter and Duff's over on straight alpha, rounded; tested by cases computed by hand. A separate mask image, DrawMask's and Image.composite's, is pending under image/mask

capability image/mask  one image laid over another through a third, a mask
  heroes  pending
  go      draw.DrawMask
  rust    -
  python  Image.composite, Image.paste with a mask, Image.putalpha
  note    -

capability image/blend  two images mixed by an amount
  heroes  image.blend
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.blend
  note    -

capability image/draw-shapes  lines, rectangles and circles drawn
  heroes  image.draw_line, image.draw_rect, image.fill_rect, image.draw_circle, image.fill_circle
  go      draw.Draw of a Uniform over a rectangle
  rust    -
  python  ImageDraw.Draw, ImageDraw.line, ImageDraw.rectangle, ImageDraw.ellipse, ImageDraw.circle
  note    one pixel wide, written with no blending, as Pillow's Draw writes on an image; the time follows the part of the shape inside the image, so a shape of any size cannot hang a program. Pillow's line width and outline width are pending under image/draw-more

capability image/draw-more  polygons, arcs, chords, pie slices, rounded rectangles, wide lines, flood fill
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageDraw.polygon, ImageDraw.regular_polygon, ImageDraw.arc, ImageDraw.chord, ImageDraw.pieslice, ImageDraw.rounded_rectangle, ImageDraw.point, ImageDraw.bitmap, ImageDraw.floodfill, ImageDraw.shape, ImagePath, line and outline width
  note    -

capability image/text  text drawn with a font
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ImageDraw.text, ImageDraw.multiline_text, ImageDraw.textbbox, ImageDraw.textlength, ImageFont, ImageFont.truetype, ImageFont.load_default
  note    a font rasterizer (TrueType's outlines, hinting, layout) is a package of its own

capability image/histogram  how many samples hold each value
  heroes  image.histogram
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.histogram, Image.entropy, ImageStat.Stat
  note    256 counts a channel, as Pillow lays them out; a 16-bit sample counts at its high byte. entropy and ImageStat's means are pending under image/statistics

capability image/statistics  extrema, colours, bounding box, means, entropy
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.getextrema, Image.getcolors, Image.getbbox, Image.entropy, ImageStat.Stat, ImageStat.Stat.mean, ImageStat.Stat.median, ImageStat.Stat.stddev
  note    -

capability image/palette  colours chosen for an image, and an image as indices into them
  heroes  image.Indexed, image.palette_of, image.to_indexed, image.from_indexed
  go      Paletted, NewPaletted, Paletted.ColorIndexAt, Paletted.SetColorIndex, color.Palette, Palette.Convert, Palette.Index, draw.FloydSteinberg, draw.Quantizer, Quantizer.Quantize
  rust    -
  python  Image.quantize, Image.convert("P"), Image.Quantize, Image.Dither, Image.getpalette, Image.putpalette, Image.remap_palette, ImagePalette
  note    median cut weighted by counts, the nearest colour by the squared differences of four channels (Go's Palette.Index uses red, green and blue and alpha in 16 bits, the same order of nearness), Floyd and Steinberg's weights as Go's documentation names them. A quantizer of the program's own would be a function value given in; median cut is the one offered

capability image/standard-palettes  palettes everybody shares
  heroes  image.web_safe_palette
  go      palette.WebSafe, palette.Plan9
  rust    -
  python  ImagePalette.ImagePalette, ImagePalette.random, ImagePalette.sepia, ImagePalette.wedge
  note    the web-safe colours in Go's order, observed. Plan 9's palette, Pillow's sepia, wedge and random are pending under image/more-palettes

capability image/more-palettes  Plan 9's palette and other made palettes
  heroes  pending
  go      palette.Plan9
  rust    -
