capability image/kind  which format a file is in, from its first bytes
  heroes  image.kind_of, image.Kind
  go      Decode's format name, DecodeConfig's format name, RegisterFormat, ErrFormat
  rust    -
  python  Image.open (format detection), Image.registered_extensions, Image.OPEN, Image.ID
  note    -

capability image/open-any  a file of any format decoded by one call
  heroes  refused: each format is a subpackage, so that a program carries only the codecs it uses (README A2); `kind_of` says which, and a program calls that format's `decode`
  go      Decode, DecodeConfig, RegisterFormat, Config
  rust    -
  python  Image.open, Image.Image.save (format by extension), Image.register_open, Image.register_save, Image.register_extension, Image.register_mime
  note    Go's registry is a mutable global filled by init functions, which the language has none of

capability image/other-formats  TIFF, WebP, ICO, AVIF, HEIF, TGA, PSD, PCX and Pillow's other formats
  heroes  pending
  go      -
